 "fixed_C0_statement": "Under HEUR-1 with the cosets fixed before inspection and T4 charged at the typical product (the run's own convention), Delta = m delta_1(C_0) = n delta_1(C_0)/C_0 grows LINEARLY in n at constant C_0, so the expected trials per relation 2^{Delta} is exp(Theta(n)) and the decompose step is not polynomial at literally constant C_0.  Polynomiality needs Delta = O(log n), i.e. C_0 >= log2 n - 2 log2 log2 n + O(1) = Theta(log n) (bound B is the 1-bit version of this), OR the searched-coset reading.",
